BND-04: book the pollutant mass carried by an outfall's reverse flow

removeOutflows() books the flow an outfall sends into the network as
external inflow, but not the pollutant mass that flow carries: the reversed
link takes the outfall's concentration (its held last value), so mass
entered the network without appearing in the quality mass balance. Book
-q * Node.newQual alongside the flow. The concentrations computed by the
model do not change.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply BND-04_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/routing.c b/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
index 9a47f4b..1aef3c1 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/routing.c
@@ -1023,7 +1023,15 @@ void removeOutflows(double tStep)
                 massbal_addOutflowQual(p, w, isFlooded);
             }
         }
-        else massbal_addInflowFlow(EXTERNAL_INFLOW, -q);
+        else
+        {
+            massbal_addInflowFlow(EXTERNAL_INFLOW, -q);
+
+            // --- pollutant mass carried into the system by an outfall's
+            //     reverse flow
+            for ( p = 0; p < Nobjects[POLLUT]; p++ )
+                massbal_addInflowQual(EXTERNAL_INFLOW, p, -q * Node[i].newQual[p]);
+        }
 
         // --- update mass balance with mass leaving system through negative
         //     lateral inflows (lateral flow was previously accounted for)
